{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bvx172w5b","tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9CpdwZqtkRSWZqHMFD4Tp","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/3d18674e-4744-4d43-ae40-96db8e6ca28e/tasks/bvx172w5b.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_4\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule` (tally span judged against a personal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, a personal left/right lean, and a shared penalty on every flip of the final run beyond the first). The one change: the edges of a sequence are salient at both ends, not only at its end — the run a sequence opens on is read first and noticed just as the run it finishes on is read last, so a sequence that starts with a streak (HHHTHT…, TTHTHH…) also looks less random, every flip of its opening run beyond the first counting against it by its own shared opening-streak penalty. Of two sequences with the same number of switches and the same ending, people therefore pick the one that starts with a switch, which the incumbent, blind to where the opening switches fall, predicts they do not.\nEOF\necho edge_streak_primacy_recency_pattern_rule > $D/model_name.txt\nsed -e 's/^\"\"\"Terminal-streak recency penalty.*/\"\"\"Edge-streak (primacy and recency) penalty on the person-specific switch-ideal rule-built judgement./' \\\n    /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule.py > $D/candidate.py\npython3 - << 'EOF'\np='/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_4/candidate.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''Refinement of `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built`: tally span judged against\na personal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching\nrate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern\nsensitivity, and a personal left/right lean. The one change: people weigh the\nflips they read last, so a sequence that ends on a streak looks less random —\nevery flip of the final run beyond the first counts against it (a shared\nterminal-streak penalty). Among equal-switch pairs people pick the sequence\nthat ends with a switch.''','''Refinement of `terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule`: tally span judged against\na personal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching\nrate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern\nsensitivity, a personal left/right lean, and a shared penalty per flip of the\nfinal run beyond the first. The one change: both edges of a sequence are\nsalient, so the run it opens on also counts — every flip of the opening run\nbeyond the first counts against it by its own shared opening-streak penalty.\nAmong equal-switch pairs people pick the sequence that starts with a switch.''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"term_diff\": terminal_excess(a) - terminal_excess(b),''','''        \"term_diff\": terminal_excess(a) - terminal_excess(b),\n        \"init_diff\": terminal_excess(a[::-1]) - terminal_excess(b[::-1]),''')\ns=s.replace('''    term_diff = pm.Data(\"term_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''','''    term_diff = pm.Data(\"term_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    init_diff = pm.Data(\"init_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''')\ns=s.replace('''    tau = pm.Normal(\"tau\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n''','''    tau = pm.Normal(\"tau\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n\n    # The change: shared penalty per flip of the opening run beyond the first.\n    tau_open = pm.Normal(\"tau_open\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n''')\ns=s.replace(